# What busybox's init does on the host: this file is laid over Alpine's own
# inittab, which starts OpenRC (not in the mini root filesystem) and puts no
# shell on a serial console. Each line is <tty>::<when>:<what>.
::sysinit:/bin/mount -t proc proc /proc
::sysinit:/bin/mount -t sysfs sysfs /sys
::sysinit:/bin/hostname socpuppet
# A shell, and no login, on hvc0, the virtio console: Linux's console on the
# host, by the decision of 2026-10-18 (docs/history/decisions.md), and where
# the exit test of M20 waits for the prompt. The leading - makes it a login
# shell, which reads /etc/profile.
hvc0::respawn:-/bin/sh
::ctrlaltdel:/sbin/reboot
::shutdown:/bin/umount -a -r
